+/* Apply an executor's source-described permissions to a referenced mm. Holes
+ * are lazy mappings and may be skipped. Unlike a native mprotect syscall this
+ * does not apply the monitor's personality, pkeys, or address untagging rules.
+ * Special mappings with callbacks/current-task assumptions are refused.
+ * The mmap write lock and normal TLB/MMU notifier path order existing PTEs. */
